{#-
  The Insights pager. Rendered twice on each page since 3 Sep 2026, at
  Bryan's request: once in the toolbar above the rows, once below them, so a
  reader who can see from the first row that this is not the page they want
  does not have to scroll ten rows to say so. Same markup both times, from
  this one file, so the two cannot drift.

  Expects `pagerSlot` in scope, "top" or "bottom". It picks the modifier class
  that positions each copy and makes the aria-label tell the two apart, so a
  screen reader's landmark list does not offer two identical "Insights
  pages" entries with no way to know which is which.

  Newer / Older rather than Previous / Next, because the list is in date
  order and that is the direction a reader is actually moving in. The step at
  either end stays in the layout as an inert span so the numbers do not
  shift sideways between the first page and the second.
-#}
<nav class="insights-pager insights-pager--{{ pagerSlot }}" aria-label="Insights pages{% if pagerSlot == 'bottom' %}, repeated below the list{% endif %}">
  {% if pagination.href.previous %}
  <a class="insights-pager-step" href="{{ pagination.href.previous }}" rel="prev">
    <span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span> Newer
  </a>
  {% else %}
  <span class="insights-pager-step is-off"><span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span> Newer</span>
  {% endif %}

  <ol class="insights-pager-numbers">
    {% for entry in pagination.pages %}
    <li>
      {% if loop.index0 == pagination.pageNumber %}
      <span class="insights-pager-num is-current" aria-current="page">{{ loop.index }}</span>
      {% else %}
      <a class="insights-pager-num" href="{{ pagination.hrefs[loop.index0] }}"
         aria-label="Page {{ loop.index }}">{{ loop.index }}</a>
      {% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>

  {% if pagination.href.next %}
  <a class="insights-pager-step" href="{{ pagination.href.next }}" rel="next">
    Older <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
  </a>
  {% else %}
  <span class="insights-pager-step is-off">Older <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
  {% endif %}
</nav>
